IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 10A — Transfer of Registration`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 10A, ss 355–364A.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- Governs re-domiciliation of foreign corporate entities as Singapore
-- companies limited by shares. Mostly procedural; this encoding covers
-- the computable deadlines.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Registration deadlines`


§§§ `s 359 — Registration and deregistration evidence`

-- s 359(6): submit deregistration evidence within 60 days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 359(6)"
`deregistration evidence days` MEANS 60

-- s 359(9): appeal period against refusal or conditions
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 359(9)"
`registration appeal days` MEANS 30


§§§ `s 362 — Revocation of registration`

-- s 362(2)(b): minimum representation period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 362(2)(b)"
`revocation representation days` MEANS 30


§§§ `s 363 — Pre-existing charges`

-- s 363(1): lodge charge particulars within 30 days of registration
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 363(1)"
`pre existing charge lodgement days` MEANS 30


§§§ `s 364 — Share certificates`

-- s 364(1): issue certificates within 60 days of registration
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 364(1)"
`transfer registration certificate days` MEANS 60

-- s 364(4): court order after 10-day default
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 364(4)"
`certificate default cure days` MEANS 10


-- ===========================================================================
-- TEST CASES
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Part 10A — Illustrations`

#ASSERT `deregistration evidence days` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `registration appeal days` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `pre existing charge lodgement days` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `transfer registration certificate days` EQUALS 60
